    "caveats": [
      "Typical values: the spread of the same season in three Mars years, not a forecast and not today's weather.",
      "Temperature is the temperature inside MEDA's humidity sensor on the rover's mast. It follows the air temperature but is not an air temperature reading; MEDA's air temperature product is not in our files. Humidity sensor data before sol 63 is not used, as the MEDA readme advises.",
      "Wind only from sols when the rover stood still, from sol 36 on; MEDA's wind sensors were damaged by wind-blown grains in 2022 and early 2023, and few sols in these windows have wind data.",
      "Measured where the rover was on those sols, 2.4 to 8.8 km from this site, at heights of -2570 to -1786 m relative to the areoid. Pressure is lower higher up."
    ],
    "productId": "MEDA data_derived_env: pressure (DER_PS), humidity sensor (DER_RHS), wind (DER_WS), ancillary (DER_ANCILLARY)",
